sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-place-08> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Because non-neuronal cells use many of the same ion-channel and electrical-synapse mechanisms as neurons for pattern formation and repair, significant commonalities may exist between the dynamics of neural networks and of bioelectric signalling networks that control shape, so neural modelling tools such as dynamic causal modelling may apply to morphogenesis data.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Neural and bioelectric patterning networks may share dynamics";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Friston K, Levin M, Sengupta B, Pezzulo G, “Knowing one's place: a free-energy approach to pattern regulation”, Journal of the Royal Society, Interface (2015), doi:10.1098/rsif.2014.1383; section “Conclusion”. Scope: Non-neural tissues with bioelectric signalling during development and regeneration"
}
